f type 1 diabetes and a mess in their  offspring however when it came to celiac  disease the results were underwhelming  and very limited so as a dietitian I'm  often asked when is the best time to  introduce gluten to my baby's diet in  order to reduce the risk of celiac  disease but what's unclear is whether or  not the exposure to gluten had a  protective effect at their lives or if  it just delayed the onset of their  diagnosis of celiac disease this is  because the researchers only followed  the babies for the first two years of  life so we need some more long-term  studies before we can make conclusive  claims while this is helpful news other  research has found that the timing of  gluten introduction has had no impact on  the risk of celiac disease in babies  having said that they did concur with  the other research suggesting that the  introduction of large amounts of gluten  may increase the risk while Peggy I hope  this information has given you a bit of  clarity  when it comes to going gluten-free  junior pregnancy and the risk of celiac  disease in your baby if you have celiac  disease then of course be sure you're  keeping a gluten-free diet for both the  health of you and your baby however if  you don't have celiac disease or gluten  intolerance I really don't see a strong  association in the literature to support  the idea of you going gluten-free if you  decide to cut out gluten be sure to  always be in the care of your doctor or  a registered dietician because cutting  out major food groups can have  implications of your baby's health and  nutrition so guys I hope you enjoyed  this video if you did be sure to give it  the thumbs up leave me a comment below  with some of your burning toilet talk  questions subscribe to the channel and  I'll see you next time on Abbey's  kitchen bye  [Music]
 

